===Noun===
{{en-noun|demonocracies}}

# {{context|fiction}} A [[government]] by [[demon]]s, whether literal (supernatural) demons or figurative demons (evil people). 
## The demonic hierarchy which governs Hell.
## The spiritual governance which demons exercise over those on earth who are in their thrall. 
## A political system some Satanists and demonolators believe will be established at the end of the age, in which all temporal powers of governance are exercised by demons, speaking through their appointed priests and priestesses on the earth. (Akin to "theocracy", except the priests are not of god but rather of demons.)
# {{pejorative}} [[democracy|Democracy]], used by those who believe that government by the people is no better than government by the devils of hell, or worse.
# {{pejorative}} used to describe the perceived misuse of the term "[[democracy|Democracy]]"

====Usage notes====
"Oppose and disagree, destroy [[demonocracy]]" is a line from the Muse song "Assassin" (on the 2006 [[w:Black Holes and Revelations|Black Holes and Revelations]] album).